4. Code rustc links into libreadcon_core.a from its standard library

rustc copies these into the static library when it builds readcon-core.
They are not in src/readcon-core/vendor. The versions are the ones rustc
1.100.0 links. A newer rustc links the versions it ships, under the same
licences. inst/licenses/readcon-sysroot holds the texts. A crate section
3 already names is not repeated, except for the version rustc links.

Rust standard library (std, core, alloc, panic_unwind, unwind,
std_detect, rustc_std_workspace_core, rustc_std_workspace_alloc), and
windows-link on Windows
  Authors: The Rust Project Contributors
  License: MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Source: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust
  The copy of backtrace compiled into std is also Apache-2.0 OR MIT,
    Copyright 2014 Alex Crichton and The Rust Project Developers.
  std/src/sync/mpmc, which the Linux static library links, is also
    Apache-2.0 OR MIT, Copyright 2019 The Crossbeam Project Developers
    and The Rust Project Developers.
  core's Unicode tables (library/core/src/unicode) are Unicode-3.0,
    Copyright 1991-2024 Unicode, Inc.

compiler_builtins 0.1.160, including its libm
  Authors: Alex Crichton, Amanieu d'Antras, Jorge Aparicio, Trevor Gross
  License: MIT AND Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception AND (MIT OR Apache-2.0).
    libm, which the static library links, is MIT. Its notices also name
    Jorge Aparicio (2018); musl (Rich Felker and others, 2005-2020); and
    math code from Sun Microsystems (1993, 2004), David Schultz
    (2003-2011), Steven G. Kargl (2003-2009), Bruce D. Evans (2003-2009),
    Stephen L. Moshier (2008), and Arm Limited (2017-2018).
  Source: https://github.com/rust-lang/compiler-builtins

